{
  "id": "ss.relic.sting",
  "name": "Stinging hairs",
  "description": "One fat segment of a caterpillar — an amber lump with a yellow-green lit back and two grooves where the next segments would join — and fifteen pale hairs standing straight out of it all the way round, no two the same length and none of them at an even angle. Each hair is a thin solid triangle with its own dark under-copy, so the whole thing silhouettes as a burr. The hairs are the relic: anything that touches you takes damage, and the fat body under them is the you. A spiky ball with even spokes read as a sun, so the hairs are jittered in length and angle and the ones underneath are a little shorter; the body is drawn as one segment rather than a caterpillar so the icon stays one object and not a small animal.",
